Voice Lab changes: cancellation at every prefill block and generated token,
explicit EOS result, greedy-only decoding, typed adapter boundary.

Voice Lab also adapts message preparation, answer parsing and Talker sampling
from MLX-Audio 0.6.3. Reference voices use its bundled CAMPPlus encoder and VAE.

Voice Lab isolates the MLX random state for model loading and each request,
exposes Talker sampling controls, and retains explicit termination evidence.
Native Ming text segmentation and per-fragment silence trimming follow
MLX-Audio's bailingmm generator. Voice Lab applies a single request-wide
acoustic-step budget and requires EOS for every fragment before completion.
